        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000004"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Oscillation is often thought of in the sense of motion, e.g., a swinging clock pendulum. However, the repetitive variation in location around a central point is technically a process of vibration, sometimes referred to as mechanical oscillation. Use the term Vibration Motion for those cases.</rdfs:comment>
